      },
      "message": "feat(motion): 2D rest area and rest pocket passes after a larger tool\n\nmachining2d::rest_plan reads what a larger previous tool could not reach\nin a pocket (the pocket minus its opening by the previous tool's disc)\nand the cutter-center area that touches it; machining2d::rest_pocket\nruns the pocket's ring passes over that area only.\n\nThe rest area is read large, never small: the cleared area is shrunk by\na margin, a corner radius and stock left on the walls count as rest\nmaterial, the allowance only grows it. The passes are the pocket's own\n(plunge and feed below the top of the cut), inside the pocket's own\ncenter area, so a wrong previous tool costs a heavier cut and never a\nrapid into stock. Refused by name: a previous tool that is not larger,\nZigzag and Adaptive with rest, nothing left to cut.\n\npocket.rs: the body of pocket() is pocket_over(), shared with the rest\npass; PocketStrategy moves to pocket_strategy.rs (structure only). The\nplain pocket posts as before.\n\nMotion crate only: the operation parameter, its undoable edit, the\nproject file, the dialog and MCP are follow-up issues.\n\nRefs #1446\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
